 "note": "builtinop.py -- read the BUILTIN-ID -> GLASM-opcode table out of the image.\n\n`f_7100f28a00` is the mapper the general builtin arm reaches:\n\n    OpExtInst -> a named intrinsic -> IR operation 0x36\n      -> f_7100f10a30's 0x36 arm passes the callee symbol's fields to\n         cg[1064][888] = f_7100fc1280\n      -> the general class arm calls f_7100fbab80\n      -> which calls profile[184] = f_7100f28a00 with W1 = the BUILTIN ID\n         (measured: 0xc24 for `max`, 0xc2c for `min`, 0x3ff for `abs`,\n          0xc9a for `sqrt`)\n\nand it ends, like every other builder, in `f_710004f530` with the GLASM opcode\nin the field-group temp's first word (notes/33).  Its switch is three jump\ntables plus a handful of direct compares; this decodes all of them.  `mask` is\nthe value it puts in `node[12]` alongside the opcode.\n\nArms that compute the opcode instead of moving a constant are reported as\n`DYN@<addr>` rather than guessed.\n",
